---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Crumbs from "../components/Crumbs.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What kinds of reports?",
    a: "It is a report that takes too long. Financial summaries, sales trackers, and operational metrics are typical. The source can be Excel, SQL, or a cloud app.",
  },
  {
    q: "How much time does my team give?",
    a: "The team gives about two to three hours for the workshop and the training. We handle the build.",
  },
  {
    q: "What happens after?",
    a: "You keep a working report and the skill to maintain it. Later add-ons can be another report, model cleanup, workspace access, or Power BI Pro licensing guidance. None of those are required to start.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do we need a Power BI license?",
    a: "We tell you if Power BI Pro is required and how to set it up.",
  },
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: SITE.url + "/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Services", item: SITE.url + "/services" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Power BI Quickstart", item: SITE.url + "/power-bi-quickstart" },
    ],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Power BI Quickstart for mid-sized firms | Alluvium"
  description="One painful report, rebuilt in two weeks. Flat fee $3,000. You get an automated Power BI report, a training session, and one week of support."
  canonicalPath="/power-bi-quickstart"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <Crumbs
          crumbs={[
            { href: "/", label: "Home" },
            { href: "/services", label: "Services" },
            { label: "Power BI Quickstart" },
          ]}
        />
        <p class="kicker">Focused engagement</p>
        <h1>Power BI Quickstart</h1>
        <p class="lede">We rebuild one painful report in two weeks. You get an automated Power BI report, a training session, and one week of support. The fee is $3,000. There is no second invoice hiding in the scope, and you are not signing up for a retainer.</p>
        <p class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/power-bi-quickstart">The Quickstart offer</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>The report that eats the week</h2>
        <p>Someone rebuilds the same pack before every meeting. Numbers move from a spreadsheet, a SQL extract, or a cloud app into slides by hand. The file is late, and two copies do not match.</p>
        <p>Quickstart takes that one report. It does not start a program, and it does not ask you to stay on after the week of support.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>What the two weeks include</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>90-minute discovery workshop</h3>
            <p>We name the report, the decision it has to support, the data, and the owner.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Data connection</h3>
            <p>We connect Excel, SQL, or a cloud app so the report is not pasted together again.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>The Power BI report</h3>
            <p>One report replaces the manual rebuild. People can filter it and trust the figure in the meeting.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Training and handoff</h3>
            <p>It is a hands-on session so your team can use the report and adjust it without us in the room.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>One week of support</h3>
            <p>After go-live we stay for troubleshooting and questions while the first real cycle runs.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Two weeks, then a week of support</h2>
        <p>Your team’s time is about two to three hours: the workshop and the training. We do the build.</p>
        <figure>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 150" role="img" aria-label="A two-week path with four stops, then a lighter week of support.">
        <line x1="36" y1="78" x2="604" y2="78" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="36" y1="78" x2="430" y2="78" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="430" y1="78" x2="604" y2="78" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="2 10" opacity="0.55"/>
        <rect x="36" y="108" width="394" height="8" rx="2" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <rect x="438" y="108" width="166" height="8" rx="2" fill="#397fb0" opacity="0.35"/>
        <circle cx="48" cy="78" r="14" fill="#fff" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="4"/>
        <circle cx="230" cy="78" r="14" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <circle cx="430" cy="78" r="14" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
        <circle cx="592" cy="78" r="14" fill="#fff" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="4"/>
        <rect x="38" y="36" width="22" height="18" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="38" y1="42" x2="60" y2="42" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="214" y="34" width="32" height="22" rx="2" fill="#e7f1f8" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="220" y1="42" x2="240" y2="42" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="220" y1="48" x2="234" y2="48" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="416" y="32" width="28" height="22" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2"/>
        <path d="M422 44 h8 M434 40 v8" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
      </svg>
          <ol class="timeline-labels">
            <li><strong>Discover.</strong> It takes ninety minutes to name the report and the owner.</li>
            <li><strong>Build.</strong> It takes about one week to connect the data and make the report.</li>
            <li><strong>Hand off.</strong> It takes one to two days of training so the team can run it.</li>
            <li><strong>Support.</strong> The week after go-live is for questions while it is in use.</li>
          </ol>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>Who it is for</h2>
        <p>It is for a mid-sized team that can point at the report, for people buried in the weekly spreadsheet, and for a leader who wants proof that Power BI is worth using, on one real file, before a larger effort.</p>
        <p>If you cannot name the report, the data, and an owner, start with Readiness and Governance Groundwork. That is not this offer under another name.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band band-alt faq" aria-labelledby="faq">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="faq">Questions</h2>
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{f.q}</summary>
            <p>{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <RelatedLinks
      services={[
        { href: "/power-bi-training", label: "Power BI training" },
        { href: "/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights", label: "Dashboard optimization" },
        { href: "/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap", label: "Analytics strategy roadmap" },
      ]}
      posts={[
        { href: "/blog/excel-vs-power-bi-financial-reporting", label: "Excel vs Power BI for financial reporting" },
        { href: "/blog/unused-power-bi-licenses", label: "Unused Power BI licenses" },
        { href: "/blog/why-month-end-still-takes-a-week", label: "Why month-end still takes a week" },
      ]}
    />

    <CtaBand
      heading="Name the one report."
      text="Book a session. We will confirm the report, the data, and the owner. That is one report, two weeks, and $3,000."
    />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .timeline-labels {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .timeline-labels li { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .timeline-labels strong { display: block; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .timeline-labels { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
</style>
